[whooping]

503
00:22:25.291 --> 00:22:27.458
No jellyfish. I promise.

504
00:22:33.041 --> 00:22:34.041
[chuckling]

505
00:22:38.541 --> 00:22:39.821
-[tense music playing]
-[screams]

506
00:22:39.875 --> 00:22:42.267
Whoa. what is it? What's the matter?
What is it? What's wrong?

507
00:22:42.291 --> 00:22:43.971
-[breathing heavily]
-[Wat] Sara. you okay?

508
00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:45.125
An eel.

509
00:22:45.208 --> 00:22:47.041
Eels in ocean. not in cave.

510
00:22:47.125 --> 00:22:48.583
I saw it. I definitely saw it.

511
00:22:49.291 --> 00:22:50.875
Many things look like eel.

512
00:22:50.958 --> 00:22:53.250
[Greg laughing loudly]

513
00:22:53.333 --> 00:22:56.000
Greg. babe. please. no.

514
00:22:56.083 --> 00:22:58.184
-[laughing] 'Cause. you know...
-[James] Uh. don't. Don't finish it.

515
00:22:58.208 --> 00:23:00.041
Don't even finish the sentence.

516
00:23:01.333 --> 00:23:03.958
[faint. indistinct chatter]

517
00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.666
[James] No turning back now.

518
00:23:07.666 --> 00:23:09.666
[mysterious music playing]

519
00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:13.625
[quiet. indistinct chatter]

520
00:23:18.625 --> 00:23:20.625
[burbling]

521
00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:29.625
[Wat] Next cave down Red Path
is very special.

522
00:23:29.708 --> 00:23:31.500
You will see.

523
00:23:31.583 --> 00:23:33.083
But no noise.

524
00:23:33.166 --> 00:23:35.875
It is the Devil's Mouth.

525
00:23:35.958 --> 00:23:39.791
Pretty sure "the Devil's Mouth" is
what the lacrosse team called Adrienne.

526
00:23:39.875 --> 00:23:41.500
Oh. you're just jealous.

527
00:23:42.916 --> 00:23:45.458
[Wat] Sara. I just wanted
to tell you something.

528
00:23:45.541 --> 00:23:50.583
Before you go under.
full exhale. then deep breath.

529
00:23:50.666 --> 00:23:51.875
Okay?

530
00:23:51.958 --> 00:23:53.958
[others chattering indistinctly]

531
00:23:59.250 --> 00:24:01.250
[atmospheric music playing]

532
00:24:25.791 --> 00:24:28.541
♪ ♪

533
00:24:28.625 --> 00:24:30.625
[indistinct chatter]

534
00:24:34.583 --> 00:24:36.375
[Wat] This is Blue Tunnel.

535
00:24:36.458 --> 00:24:38.541
Sunlight hits white sand.

536
00:24:38.625 --> 00:24:40.125
Shows us the way home.

537
00:24:40.208 --> 00:24:42.583
[Max] Tunnel means exit. Got it.

538
00:24:42.666 --> 00:24:44.666
[tranquil music playing]

539
00:24:46.916 --> 00:24:48.416
Wow.

540
00:24:52.125 --> 00:24:53.601
[Greg] This is the coolest cave ever.

541
00:24:53.625 --> 00:24:55.541
Shh.

542
00:24:55.625 --> 00:24:57.666
-[James] S-Sorry.
-[Greg] Sorry.

543
00:24:59.166 --> 00:25:00.625
-[thuds]
-Ow.

544
00:25:00.708 --> 00:25:02.208
Freaking Red Path.

545
00:25:04.583 --> 00:25:06.583
[mysterious music playing]

546
00:25:11.291 --> 00:25:12.708
[James] Whoa.

547
00:25:12.791 --> 00:25:14.083
[Max] Wow.

548
00:25:14.166 --> 00:25:16.416
This is Devil's Mouth.

549
00:25:16.500 --> 00:25:18.041
See?

550
00:25:18.125 --> 00:25:19.250
Teeth.

551
00:25:21.916 --> 00:25:23.916
[bats squeaking]

552
00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.000
[wings fluttering]

553
00:25:44.083 --> 00:25:45.500
-[wings fluttering]
-[screams]

554
00:25:45.583 --> 00:25:47.375
[bats squeaking]

555
00:25:47.458 --> 00:25:48.916
[Wat] Shh.

556
00:25:50.541 --> 00:25:52.541
[quiet. indistinct chatter]

557
00:25:57.583 --> 00:25:59.375
[whistles]

558
00:25:59.458 --> 00:26:02.458
-[bats squeaking frantically]
-[dramatic music playing]

559
00:26:13.250 --> 00:26:14.708
Sara. hurry.

560
00:26:15.375 --> 00:26:17.250
Kind of cool. actually.

561
00:26:20.416 --> 00:26:22.166
[gasps]

562
00:26:22.250 --> 00:26:24.166
Wait. Max. [grunts]

563
00:26:24.250 --> 00:26:25.416
[tense music playing]

564
00:26:25.500 --> 00:26:27.625
[grunts. breathes heavily]

565
00:26:39.166 --> 00:26:40.791
[sighs]

566
00:26:42.958 --> 00:26:45.000
Ah. Sara. you okay?

567
00:26:45.083 --> 00:26:46.083
Yeah. I'm good.

568
00:26:46.166 --> 00:26:48.916
This is the Skeleton Cave.

569
00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:50.833
Real bones below.

570
00:26:50.916 --> 00:26:52.625
Human? Animal?

571
00:26:52.708 --> 00:26:54.083
-Yes. Human.
-[James clears throat]

572
00:26:54.166 --> 00:26:56.166
-Wat.
-Yes?

573
00:26:56.250 --> 00:26:58.666
-You said "human bones."
-Mm-hmm.

574
00:26:58.750 --> 00:27:00.291
What? Why?

575
00:27:00.375 --> 00:27:02.375
These caves. they're very old.

576
00:27:03.416 --> 00:27:04.625
Many. many years.

577
00:27:04.708 --> 00:27:07.291
Sinkhole and boom.

578
00:27:07.375 --> 00:27:09.125
Whole village die.

579
00:27:09.208 --> 00:27:11.291
We are guests here.

580
00:27:11.375 --> 00:27:13.333
Caves are master.

581
00:27:13.416 --> 00:27:14.833
If you do not respect the caves...

582
00:27:14.916 --> 00:27:17.416
James. the bone cave?

583
00:27:17.500 --> 00:27:18.916
-Get it. bro?
-[Wat] Hey.

584
00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:20.583
-[laughing] The bone cave?
-[Wat] Hey.

585
00:27:20.666 --> 00:27:22.708
This is no joke.

586
00:27:22.791 --> 00:27:24.791
[quiet. indistinct chatter]

587
00:27:27.375 --> 00:27:29.375
[Max] You okay? It's okay.

588
00:27:29.458 --> 00:27:30.958
God. James. Come on.

589
00:27:31.041 --> 00:27:32.291
Human bones.

590
00:27:32.375 --> 00:27:34.625
[Max] They're already dead.
They're already dead.

591
00:27:34.708 --> 00:27:36.708
[mysterious music playing]

592
00:27:49.250 --> 00:27:51.250
-[Adrienne] Sara! We have an emergency!
-[gasps]

593
00:27:51.333 --> 00:27:52.875
Emergency photo op.

594
00:27:52.958 --> 00:27:54.875
-[chuckling]
-Come on.

595
00:27:54.958 --> 00:27:56.500
[Wat] Here. I'll take for you.

596
00:27:56.583 --> 00:27:58.041
[Greg] Start flexing. James.

597
00:27:58.125 --> 00:27:59.666
-[quiet. indistinct chatter]
-[grunts]

598
00:27:59.750 --> 00:28:01.541
-[Wat] Okay. ready?
-[Sara] Okay.

599
00:28:01.625 --> 00:28:03.833
One. two. three.

600
00:28:03.916 --> 00:28:06.000
[camera click echoes]

601
00:28:06.083 --> 00:28:07.083
[Max] Great.

602
00:28:07.166 --> 00:28:10.416
-Now we have Greg in our memories forever.
-Yeah.

603
00:28:10.500 --> 00:28:12.767
-[Adrienne] That's funny. yeah.
-[Max] Uh. I want you to shoot up.

604
00:28:12.791 --> 00:28:15.416
-[Adrienne] Okay.
-[James] Phi Beta Kappa.

605
00:28:15.500 --> 00:28:18.041
You'd think he'd understand
what "respect the caves" means.

606
00:28:18.125 --> 00:28:19.958
Ow. Greg. Greg!

607
00:28:20.041 --> 00:28:22.458
He should really point his toes more.

608
00:28:22.541 --> 00:28:25.291
-[indistinct chatter]
-[Sara] Max. the director.

609
00:28:25.375 --> 00:28:28.500
-Taking charge since sophomore year.
-Mm-hmm.

610
00:28:28.583 --> 00:28:30.666
How did we survive without her?

611
00:28:35.583 --> 00:28:36.916
-[grunts]
-[others scream]

612
00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:39.708
Hey. What'd I tell you?

613
00:28:39.791 --> 00:28:41.291
This rock very weak.

614
00:28:41.375 --> 00:28:43.166
You cause collapse. we die.

615
00:28:43.250 --> 00:28:45.333
Yeah. yeah. I'm sorry. It was an accident.

616
00:28:45.416 --> 00:28:47.000
-I-I didn't mean to.
-[snickers]

617
00:28:47.083 --> 00:28:48.125
[Wat] We go now.

618
00:28:48.208 --> 00:28:49.500
Next cave.

619
00:28:49.583 --> 00:28:50.666
[quiet laughter]

620
00:28:50.750 --> 00:28:52.625
Wh-What?

621
00:28:52.708 --> 00:28:54.708
Ooh. you got yelled at.

622
00:28:54.791 --> 00:28:57.666
[quiet. indistinct chatter]

623
00:28:57.750 --> 00:28:59.750
[foreboding music playing]

624
00:29:07.583 --> 00:29:09.583
[indistinct chatter continues]

625
00:29:13.958 --> 00:29:15.583
What is that?

626
00:29:15.666 --> 00:29:18.000
[James] What? What is it?

627
00:29:18.083 --> 00:29:20.166
[Greg] What's that smell?

628
00:29:20.250 --> 00:29:22.166
Ew.

629
00:29:22.250 --> 00:29:24.625
[Wat] These are saltwater fish
from the ocean.

630
00:29:24.708 --> 00:29:25.875
[James] The hell?

631
00:29:25.958 --> 00:29:28.208
Uh. all these fish are dead.

632
00:29:34.625 --> 00:29:37.708
Baby. will you cancel
our sushi plans tonight?

633
00:29:40.625 --> 00:29:42.458
How did they even get in here?

634
00:29:44.583 --> 00:29:47.750
[Sara] That cave opens to the ocean
through that passage.

635
00:29:47.833 --> 00:29:48.958
[Wat] Yes.

636
00:29:49.541 --> 00:29:50.916
But the opening is very high.

637
00:29:51.750 --> 00:29:53.041
Too high.

638
00:29:53.125 --> 00:29:56.000
The storm could have flooded
the ocean water in here.

639
00:29:56.083 --> 00:29:58.750
Then the fresh water killed
all the sea life.

640
00:29:58.833 --> 00:30:01.166
Uh. should we turn around?

641
00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:02.666
[Wat] Uh...

642
00:30:03.833 --> 00:30:05.541
I take you back a different way.

643
00:30:05.625 --> 00:30:07.875
We go this way. Next cave.

644
00:30:10.458 --> 00:30:12.541
You okay?

645
00:30:12.625 --> 00:30:14.125
You can come with me.

646
00:30:14.208 --> 00:30:15.750
Yeah. I'm fine.

647
00:30:15.833 --> 00:30:17.791
Hey. Wat. what's with
all the special attention?

648
00:30:17.875 --> 00:30:21.375
Uh. your friend. she tip extra.

649
00:30:21.458 --> 00:30:23.875
say that you need extra care.

650
00:30:23.958 --> 00:30:25.166
I'm fine.

651
00:30:25.250 --> 00:30:27.458
I paid for the trip.
so I'm the one who tips.

652
00:30:27.541 --> 00:30:29.166
No more special treatment. okay?

653
00:30:29.250 --> 00:30:31.250
-Okay. Yes.
-Thank you.

654
00:30:33.833 --> 00:30:36.583
[others chattering indistinctly]

655
00:30:48.250 --> 00:30:50.250
[burbling]

656
00:30:53.375 --> 00:30:55.500
[tense music playing]

657
00:30:55.583 --> 00:30:57.166
[gasps] Geez.

658
00:30:57.250 --> 00:30:58.666
[exhales heavily]

659
00:31:05.125 --> 00:31:07.125
[ominous music playing]

660
00:31:20.333 --> 00:31:22.208
This is sick.

661
00:31:22.291 --> 00:31:23.625
Whoa.

662
00:31:26.208 --> 00:31:27.500
Wow.

663
00:31:27.583 --> 00:31:29.583
[quiet. indistinct chatter]

664
00:31:36.333 --> 00:31:38.333
-[Sara grunts]
-[Max] How are the welts?

665
00:31:39.416 --> 00:31:41.958
Fine. Fresh water doesn't sting as much.

666
00:31:42.041 --> 00:31:44.375
-Yeah.
-Is that why you put Wat on me?

667
00:31:44.458 --> 00:31:45.500
What?

668
00:31:45.583 --> 00:31:47.351
-He told me about your little tip.
-Well. babe.

669
00:31:47.375 --> 00:31:49.851
you made such a big deal about me. like.
not looking out for you the other day.

670
00:31:49.875 --> 00:31:50.875
I just thought...

671
00:31:50.958 --> 00:31:52.541
Pay someone to infantilize me?

672
00:31:53.916 --> 00:31:56.125
Sara. give me your knife.

673
00:31:58.666 --> 00:31:59.875
Gonna fight to the death?

674
00:31:59.958 --> 00:32:01.958
[others chattering indistinctly]

675
00:32:02.041 --> 00:32:04.041
[atmospheric music playing]

676
00:32:17.458 --> 00:32:18.916
-[Sara] Max.
-[Max laughs]

677
00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:20.500
Now it's carved in stone.

678
00:32:20.583 --> 00:32:22.125
You're stuck with me. Boom!

679
00:32:22.208 --> 00:32:24.666
[muffled splashing]

680
00:32:24.750 --> 00:32:26.958
-Okay. cheeseball!
-[Max laughing]

681
00:32:28.250 --> 00:32:29.958
Gay!

682
00:32:31.916 --> 00:32:33.583
-[screams]
-What? What?

683
00:32:33.666 --> 00:32:36.000
I felt something on my fin.

684
00:32:36.083 --> 00:32:38.958
[breathing heavily]

685
00:32:39.041 --> 00:32:41.166
I don't see anything.

686
00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:44.416
Hey. uh. it's okay.

687
00:32:44.500 --> 00:32:47.083
-Yeah.
-It's good. Come on. let's go.

688
00:32:47.166 --> 00:32:49.208
Hey. come on.

689
00:32:49.291 --> 00:32:50.708
It's okay.

690
00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:03.625
Rocks are sharp. Go slow.

691
00:33:09.291 --> 00:33:12.708
It's amazing how old they are
and still so fragile.

692
00:33:12.791 --> 00:33:15.083
Limestone sinkhole.

693
00:33:15.166 --> 00:33:17.541
-That's how the caves are formed.
-[Greg] Limestone.

694
00:33:17.625 --> 00:33:19.333
Carbonate sedimentary.

695
00:33:19.416 --> 00:33:22.250
Let me guess: rocks for jocks?

696
00:33:22.333 --> 00:33:23.750
[laughing] You know it. baby.

697
00:33:23.833 --> 00:33:25.416
It's my first A.

698
00:33:25.500 --> 00:33:26.916
-[James] Uh...
-Minus. minus.

699
00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:37.000
[Adrienne whimpers]

700
00:33:37.083 --> 00:33:38.892
-Oh. damn. One of them cut me.
-What's... What...

701
00:33:38.916 --> 00:33:40.666
Oh. no. no. no. no. I can't look.

702
00:33:40.750 --> 00:33:41.833
Come on. come on.

703
00:33:41.916 --> 00:33:43.750
Oh. I can't look.
I can't look. I can't look.

704
00:33:43.833 --> 00:33:46.625
There's damn knives all under us.

705
00:33:46.708 --> 00:33:48.791
Are you good. Cousin Greg?

706
00:33:48.875 --> 00:33:52.125
[Adrienne] Oh. oh. right.
Uh. he has this thing about blood.

707
00:33:52.208 --> 00:33:53.958
Uh. babe. remember the mantra?

708
00:33:54.041 --> 00:33:55.500
-What's his thing about blood?
-Yeah.

709
00:33:55.583 --> 00:33:56.791
He can't be around it.

710
00:33:56.875 --> 00:34:01.291
-"I am safe. I am special. I am me."
-Yeah. Yeah. I'm me.

711
00:34:01.375 --> 00:34:02.916
Oh. my God. no.

712
00:34:03.625 --> 00:34:05.541
-No.
-[James] Seriously. though. Greg.

713
00:34:05.625 --> 00:34:07.265
-you all right. bud?
-Is it... is it done?

714
00:34:07.291 --> 00:34:09.333
Th-The blood. did she s-stop bleeding?

715
00:34:09.416 --> 00:34:11.083
[Sara] Can you guys calm him down?

716
00:34:11.166 --> 00:34:14.291
"I am safe. I am special. I am..."
wh-whatever.

717
00:34:14.375 --> 00:34:16.434
[Greg] Well. when I was a kid.
my brother pranked me.

718
00:34:16.458 --> 00:34:21.416
It was a fake bike accident with
our neighbor Tanner. who was like five.

719
00:34:21.500 --> 00:34:23.500
-He used ketchup as blood.
-[chuckles] Classic.

720
00:34:23.583 --> 00:34:25.291
Well. it totally traumatized me.

721
00:34:25.375 --> 00:34:27.916
Now. whenever I'm around blood.
I-I... I panic.

722
00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:29.208
Now all I see is dead Tan-Tan.

723
00:34:30.041 --> 00:34:32.250
[Sara] That tape should hold.
Do you want to keep going?

724
00:34:32.333 --> 00:34:34.000
[Wat] No. no. no. no. Policy is.

725
00:34:34.083 --> 00:34:37.541
if any injury. we return.
so we go back now.

726
00:34:37.625 --> 00:34:39.708
Okay. well. well. wait. wait. wait. wait.

727
00:34:39.791 --> 00:34:42.541
Adrienne. babe. you're fine. right?

728
00:34:42.625 --> 00:34:44.583
Your concern for me is touching.
It really is.

729
00:34:44.666 --> 00:34:47.708
I just read that the last cave is.
like. a cannot-miss. you guys.

730
00:34:47.791 --> 00:34:49.000
Max. she is bleeding.

731
00:34:50.791 --> 00:34:52.791
Okay. How about this?

732
00:34:53.583 --> 00:34:56.625
You guys start going back. and I'm gonna
go check out the cave really quick.

733
00:34:56.708 --> 00:34:58.726
and I'll swim really fast
and catch up with you guys.

734
00:34:58.750 --> 00:35:00.434
You're gonna go check out
the last cave by yourself?

735
00:35:00.458 --> 00:35:03.708
-Yep.
-Wat. is that even safe?

736
00:35:03.791 --> 00:35:06.125
[Wat] No. no. no. not safe.

737
00:35:06.208 --> 00:35:08.208
[atmospheric music playing]

738
00:35:22.625 --> 00:35:24.625
[tense music playing]

739
00:35:35.208 --> 00:35:37.684
-[Max] Why shouldn't I do that. right?
-[Adrienne] No. no. no. Hey. hey. hey.

740
00:35:37.708 --> 00:35:39.059
-What?
-[Adrienne] I'm fine. I'm fine.

741
00:35:39.083 --> 00:35:43.458
Let's just go to the next one... together.

742
00:35:43.541 --> 00:35:44.583
Yay!

743
00:35:45.291 --> 00:35:47.541
[in Thai] Better get
a good tip for this shit.

744
00:35:49.458 --> 00:35:50.658
[in English] Wh-What'd he say?

745
00:35:50.708 --> 00:35:53.458
All right. um. Greg. Hi. babe. Look at me.

746
00:35:53.541 --> 00:35:56.166
No more blood. Everything is okay.

747
00:35:56.250 --> 00:35:57.625
I am safe.

748
00:35:57.708 --> 00:36:00.041
-I am special.
-I am special.

749
00:36:00.125 --> 00:36:01.333
[both] I am me.

750
00:36:01.416 --> 00:36:03.083
Okay. you assholes. All together.

751
00:36:03.166 --> 00:36:04.666
-I am safe.
-[Greg] I'm safe.

752
00:36:04.750 --> 00:36:06.416
[Adrienne. Max and Greg] I am special.

753
00:36:06.500 --> 00:36:08.458
[Adrienne. Max. Greg and Sara] I am me.

754
00:36:08.541 --> 00:36:10.416
[atmospheric music playing]

755
00:36:10.500 --> 00:36:13.208
[Adrienne] Okay. this is it.

756
00:36:13.291 --> 00:36:15.958
-Better be worth it.
-[James] I don't see anything yet.

757
00:36:21.708 --> 00:36:23.125
[Wat] Lights off.

758
00:36:23.208 --> 00:36:24.833
[Max] Guys. lights off.

759
00:36:24.916 --> 00:36:26.833
